{"id":"6e978b1f-2e7c-41b0-935a-c163f5d7df28","object":"chat.completion","created":1784997669,"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\n  \"implementation\": \"import math\\ndef solve(case):\\n    if 'matrix' not in case:\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"Missing 'matrix' key\\\")\\n    matrix = case['matrix']\\n    if not isinstance(matrix, list) or len(matrix) == 0:\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"matrix must be a non-empty list\\\")\\n    n_rows = len(matrix)\\n    n_cols = None\\n    for row in matrix:\\n        if not isinstance(row, list):\\n            raise ValueError(\\\"Each row must be a list\\\")\\n        if n_cols is None:\\n            n_cols = len(row)\\n        elif len(row) != n_cols:\\n            raise ValueError(\\\"Matrix rows must have same length\\\")\\n    if n_cols == 0:\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"Matrix must have at least one column\\\")\\n    df = [0] * n_cols\\n    for row in matrix:\\n        for j, val in enumerate(row):\\n            if val != 0:\\n                df[j] += 1\\n    idf = []\\n    for j in range(n_cols):\\n        idf_val = math.log(1 + n_rows / (1 + df[j]))\\n        idf.append(round(idf_val, 6))\\n    weighted_matrix = []\\n    row_degree = []\\n    for i in range(n_rows):\\n        weighted_row = []\\n        row_sum = 0.0\\n        for j in range(n_cols):\\n            w = matrix[i][j] * idf[j]\\n            weighted_row.append(round(w, 6))\\n            row_sum += w\\n        weighted_matrix.append(weighted_row)\\n        row_degree.append(round(row_sum, 6))\\n    return {\\n        \\\"idf\\\": idf,\\n        \\\"weighted_matrix\\\": weighted_matrix,\\n        \\\"row_degree\\\": row_degree\\n    }\"\n}","reasoning_content":"We need to write a Python function `solve(case)` that takes a payload object (with a `matrix` field and possibly `_case_nonce`). The task is to compute IDF normalization and row degree. The output schema is given: an object with keys \"idf\" (